  "caption": "You booked the room, then the hotel asks for a few more euros at the desk. That's usually the city tax.\n\nMany cities and regions charge a small local tax per person, per night. The city sets it, not the hotel, and it's often collected on site at check-in or checkout. In some places it depends on the hotel's star rating, and children can be exempt. Look for \"payable at the property\" in your booking details.\n\nSave this for your next city break.\n\n#hotelbooking #traveltips #citybreak",
